VeridianOS: tablet KCM: free the libwacom device in TabletsModel::data()

Real bug, found while preparing 0003's libwacom fix for upstream
(invent.kde.org/plasma/plasma-desktop): TabletsModel::data() creates a
WacomDevice with libwacom_new_from_path() for every display-role request
and returned its name without libwacom_destroy(), leaking a device each
time the list is painted. The name is copied into a QString and the
device destroyed.

--- a/kcms/tablet/tabletsmodel.cpp
+++ b/kcms/tablet/tabletsmodel.cpp
@@ -78,7 +78,9 @@
             libwacom_error_free(&error);
         } else {
             libwacom_error_free(&error);
-            return libwacom_get_name(device);
+            const QString name = QString::fromUtf8(libwacom_get_name(device));
+            libwacom_destroy(device);
+            return name;
         }
 
         if (hasPenDevice) {
